&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Druva&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Druva is the resilience foundation for the AI enterprise, helping organizations secure and recover from connected risk across data, cyber, identity, and AI. The Resilience Cloud is a fully managed, cloud-native SaaS platform that delivers air-gapped and immutable protection across cloud, SaaS, on-premises, endpoint, and edge environments. Powered by Dru MetaGraph, Druva’s graph-powered intelligence layer, the platform connects critical business context so customers can understand risk, respond faster, recover cleanly, and govern data with greater confidence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Trusted by nearly 7,500 customers, including 75 of the Fortune 500, Druva helps safeguard the critical information and systems businesses depend on in an increasingly connected world.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Visit&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.druva.com/&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;druva.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and follow us on&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/druva/mycompany/&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/druvainc&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/DruvaInc/&quot;&gt;Facebook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits on a highly collaborative, performance-driven sales team focused on helping customers modernize data protection and cyber resilience with Druva’s 100% SaaS platform. The Account Executive owns the territory end-to-end, maintaining and expanding existing customer relationships and renewals while actively hunting and closing net-new logos.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work in a true two-in-a-box model with a dedicated local Systems Engineer to drive deep discovery, strong customer engagement, and a consultative sales motion across the full lifecycle, from prospecting through expansion. This is a high-impact role for someone who thrives on territory ownership, values teamwork, and enjoys building durable customer relationships while driving new growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Purpose &amp;amp; Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own and execute the go-to-market strategy for the assigned LATAM territory, managing a defined book of business while identifying, prospecting, and closing new customer opportunities across organizations in LATAM.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will build trusted relationships with IT and security leaders by understanding their business challenges and aligning them to Druva’s cloud-native data protection and cyber resilience platform. Partnering closely with a dedicated local Systems Engineer, you will lead discovery, technical validation, and solution design to clearly articulate the value of a SaaS-based approach.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will collaborate cross-functionally with Customer Success, Channel Partners, and internal teams to support onboarding, adoption, renewals, and expansion, while building pipeline, forecasting accurately, and consistently delivering against revenue targets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prospect and close new sales opportunities in a defined territory and a defined set of target accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate results; consistent, reliable performance with 100% minimum attainment expected&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the local, regional and national channel partners to drive awareness and &quot;buzz&quot; in your territory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Arrange and help conduct initial product demonstrations and presentations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage sales process and opportunity closure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ongoing account management to ensure customer satisfaction and to drive additional cross-sell/up-sell opportunities and renewals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes You a Great Fit&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of Field Account Executive experience with documented quota attainment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in English, Spanish and Portuguese&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sales experience in the IT or technology industry preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build executive-level relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous learner and student of the game - you want to constantly get better&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand the &quot;bigger picture&quot; and the business drivers around IT&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You strive for greatness and push yourself&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to professionalism, integrity, and positive team culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s Degree or equivalent&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like in this Role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success means consistently owning and growing the assigned territory through predictable, high-quality execution. You effectively balance expanding existing accounts with adding new logos, building trusted relationships with IT and security leaders and positioning Druva as a strategic partner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You operate as a strong partner to your dedicated Systems Engineer, lead disciplined discovery, guide customers through value-based buying decisions, and maintain a healthy, well-managed pipeline with accurate forecasts. You collaborate closely with Customer Success and channel partners to drive renewals, expansions, and long-term retention.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are also a dependable, high-integrity team member who shows up prepared, contributes to a strong team culture, and helps elevate the overall performance of the Commercial Central Team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You’ll Love Working Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Innovation is how we operate, not a side project. You’ll work in a culture that values bold thinking and continuous improvement, where global teams experiment, iterate, and turn new ideas into products customers can rely on.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re looking for high-ownership work, visible impact, and a culture that values innovation, collaboration, accountability, and growth—where you’ll be trusted to lead and empowered to build—you’ll thrive at Druva.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The pay range for this position is expected to be between &lt;strong&gt;$140,000 and $187,333/year;&lt;/strong&gt; however, base pay offered may vary depending on multiple individualized, non-discriminatory factors, including market location, job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. The total compensation package for this position may also include other incentive compensation opportunities in the form of discretionary annual bonus or commissions, and equity. Additionally, full-time employees are eligible to participate in our comprehensive benefits program, including health and wellness benefits, 401(k) retirement plan, life and disability insurance coverages, and other benefits the Company may offer from time to time.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Data Privacy Notice for Job Candidates:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For information on personal data processing, please see our &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.druva.com/privacy-policy&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Druva Privacy Policy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Druva is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin or nationality, ancestry, age, disability, gender identity or expression, marital status, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you are an individual with a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to complete any part of the application process, or are limited in the ability or unable to access or use this online application process and need an alternative method for applying, you may contact us at &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruiting_us@druva.com&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;recruiting_us@druva.com&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12ScreenRdr.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;EEO IS THE LAW&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.dol.gov/sites/dolgov/files/olms/regs/compliance/eo_posters/employeerightsposter2page_19final.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;NOTIFICATION OF EMPLOYEE RIGHTS UNDER FEDERAL LABOR LAWS&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;**If you’re interested in joining the Druva family in a future Sales/Account Executive role in the San Francisco Bay Area, please join our talent community. Submit your resume below, and a recruiter will review and reach out when we have an opportunity arise that matches your skillset &amp;amp; interests. This post is not in reference to a currently open position, but rather in anticipation of future business need.**&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Druva enables cyber, data and operational resilience for every organization with the Data Resiliency Cloud, the industry’s first and only at scale SaaS solution. Customers can radically simplify data protection, streamline data governance, and gain data visibility and insights as they accelerate cloud adoption. Druva pioneered a SaaS-based approach to eliminate complex infrastructure and related management costs, and deliver data resilience via a single platform spanning multiple geographies and clouds. Druva is trusted by thousands of enterprises, including 60 of Fortune 500, to make data more resilient and accelerate their journey to the cloud. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Visit &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.druva.com/&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;druva.com&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; and follow us on &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/druva/mycompany/&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/druvainc&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/DruvaInc/&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Facebook&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Druva&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Druva is the resilience foundation for the AI enterprise, helping organizations secure and recover from connected risk across data, cyber, identity, and AI. The Resilience Cloud is a fully managed, cloud-native SaaS platform that delivers air-gapped and immutable protection across cloud, SaaS, on-premises, endpoint, and edge environments. Powered by Dru MetaGraph, Druva’s graph-powered intelligence layer, the platform connects critical business context so customers can understand risk, respond faster, recover cleanly, and govern data with greater confidence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Trusted by nearly 7,500 customers, including 75 of the Fortune 500, Druva helps safeguard the critical information and systems businesses depend on in an increasingly connected world.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Visit&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.druva.com/&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;druva.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and follow us on&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/druva/mycompany/&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/druvainc&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/DruvaInc/&quot;&gt;Facebook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Cloud Operations Engineer at Druva, the industry leader in Cloud Data Protection and Management, you will play a key role in supporting, maintaining, and scaling cloud infrastructure within a fast-paced, complex, and FedRAMP-certified environment. Working under general guidance, your focus will be on developing professional expertise in cloud operations, addressing tasks of moderate scope, proactive monitoring, and assisting cross-functional teams to deliver reliable, highly available solutions for our growing customer community.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in weekly team meetings, working closely with devops, support, and quality assurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and manage all cloud infrastructure, including Friday evening deployments of&amp;nbsp;production updates and OS patches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support various AWS and Azure services being utilized and gain foundational expertise&amp;nbsp;across primary infrastructure components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Incident Response and Troubleshooting:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize and address tickets related to server, network, and storage issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide escalated support for problems and incidents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure incident resolution is within the defined SLA (Service Level Agreement)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automation and Monitoring:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, maintain, and enhance Infrastructure as Code (e.g., Terraform,&amp;nbsp;CloudFormation) and automation scripts for testing and deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure and deploy supporting tools for proactive monitoring, observability, and&amp;nbsp;security (e.g., Grafana, Prometheus/Thanos, Wiz, OpenSearch)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication and Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively communicate project updates and tasks to the Operations team and&amp;nbsp;stakeholders in other departments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional teams to ensure seamless cloud operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expectations:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support production deployments scheduled on Fridays between 5pm - 11pm PDT on a rotating&amp;nbsp;basis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take responsibility for identifying and resolving vulnerabilities in the FedRAMP environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and monitor dashboards to track real-time metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience &amp;amp; Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 2 years of related experience (or an advanced degree without&amp;nbsp;experience, or equivalent work experience)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in AWS and Azure services (or another Cloud Provider).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with containerized applications (ECS, Kubernetes, Docker)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with observability and monitoring (Grafana, OpenSearch)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with an SIEM (Security Incident and Event Management) application&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with one programming language (Python, Go)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with Infrastructure as Code (Terraform, CloudFormation)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Linux operating systems deployments &amp;amp; patching (Ubuntu, RHEL)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;&quot; data-bfc=&quot;&quot; data-sfc-cp=&quot;&quot; data-sfc-root=&quot;ep&quot; data-ved=&quot;2ahUKEwi2wd7H_5GXAxURrIkEHdIYKMoQi4wTegoIAAgACAEIDRAF&quot; data-hveid=&quot;CAAIAAgBCA0QBQ&quot; data-copy-service-computed-style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans&amp;quot;, Roboto, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;iNqyIf&quot; data-sfc-cp=&quot;&quot; data-sfc-root=&quot;ep&quot; data-copy-service-computed-style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans&amp;quot;, Roboto, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot;&gt;U.S. citizenship is required to support Federal customer engagements. Existing or ability to obtain a U.S. government security clearance (Public Trust, Secret, or higher) is a strong plus.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong class=&quot;rQesXe MPyX&quot; data-sfc-cp=&quot;&quot; data-sfc-root=&quot;ep&quot; data-copy-service-computed-style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans&amp;quot;, Roboto, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;yhAwj&quot; data-sfc-cp=&quot;&quot; data-sfc-root=&quot;ep&quot; data-sfc-inited=&quot;2&quot; data-copy-service-computed-style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans&amp;quot;, Roboto, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;&quot; data-bfc=&quot;&quot; data-sfc-cp=&quot;&quot; data-sfc-root=&quot;ep&quot; data-ved=&quot;2ahUKEwi2wd7H_5GXAxURrIkEHdIYKMoQi4wTegoIAAgACAEIDhAA&quot; data-hveid=&quot;CAAIAAgBCA4QAA&quot; data-copy-service-computed-style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans&amp;quot;, Roboto, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;AHmQrc&quot; data-sfc-cp=&quot;&quot; data-sfc-root=&quot;ep&quot; data-hveid=&quot;CAAIAAgBCA4QAQ&quot; data-copy-service-computed-style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans&amp;quot;, Roboto, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 0px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;n6owBd awi2gc&quot; data-sfc-cp=&quot;&quot; data-sfc-root=&quot;ep&quot; data-hveid=&quot;CAAIAAgBCA4QAg&quot; data-copy-service-computed-style=&quot;font-family: &amp;quot;Google Sans&amp;quot;, Roboto, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 400; margin: 12px 0px 16px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 0px rgb(10, 10, 10);&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Certifications (Bonus):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AWS, Azure, RHEL, CCNA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You’ll Love Working Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Innovation is how we operate, not a side project. You’ll work in a culture that values bold thinking and continuous improvement, where global teams experiment, iterate, and turn new ideas into products customers can rely on.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re looking for high-ownership work, visible impact, and a culture that values innovation, collaboration, accountability, and growth—where you’ll be trusted to lead and empowered to build—you’ll thrive at Druva.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The pay range for this position is expected to be between &lt;strong&gt;$108,000 and $151,333/year;&lt;/strong&gt; however, base pay offered may vary depending on multiple individualized, non-discriminatory factors, including market location, job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. The total compensation package for this position may also include other incentive compensation opportunities in the form of discretionary annual bonus or commissions, and equity. Additionally, full-time employees are eligible to participate in our comprehensive benefits program, including health and wellness benefits, 401(k) retirement plan, life and disability insurance coverages, and other benefits the Company may offer from time to time.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Data Privacy Notice for Job Candidates:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For information on personal data processing, please see our &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.druva.com/privacy-policy&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Druva Privacy Policy&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Druva is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin or nationality, ancestry, age, disability, gender identity or expression, marital status, veteran status, or any other category protected by law.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you are an individual with a disability and require a reasonable accommodation to complete any part of the application process, or are limited in the ability or unable to access or use this online application process and need an alternative method for applying, you may contact us at &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruiting_us@druva.com&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;recruiting_us@druva.com&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12ScreenRdr.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;EEO IS THE LAW&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.dol.gov/sites/dolgov/files/olms/regs/compliance/eo_posters/employeerightsposter2page_19final.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;NOTIFICATION OF EMPLOYEE RIGHTS UNDER FEDERAL LABOR LAWS&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Druva is seeking an MSP Metering &amp;amp; Data Operations Manager to own the operational administration, data integrity, reporting, and forecasting capabilities supporting our global Managed Service Provider business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will serve as the operational owner of the m3ter metering platform and the data flows that underpin MSP consumption, billing, forecasting, and business performance reporting. The successful candidate will combine strong data-analysis skills with hands-on platform administration and business acumen.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The primary objective is simple: ensure MSP consumption data is accurate, explainable, actionable, and trusted across the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;m3ter Platform Administration&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- m3ter Platform Administration&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Serve as the primary business administrator and subject-matter expert for the m3ter platform supporting Druva&#39;s MSP consumption model.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Configure and maintain meters, products, pricing structures, account mappings, and related platform components.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Monitor ingestion and processing of MSP consumption data and identify anomalies, failures, or unexpected results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Coordinate changes to metering logic as Druva introduces new products, SKUs, consumption models, partners, and commercial programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Maintain appropriate documentation, controls, and operating procedures for m3ter administration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Partner with Finance, Deal Desk, Product, Engineering, RevOps, and MSP leadership to ensure metering logic accurately reflects commercial agreements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Data Monitoring &amp;amp; Issue Resolution&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Proactively monitor MSP consumption and metering data for completeness, accuracy, and consistency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Identify discrepancies between source telemetry, m3ter, CRM, billing, and reporting systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Diagnose data issues and determine whether root causes originate from source data, ingestion, mapping, transformation, metering configuration, or reporting logic.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Coordinate resolution with Engineering, Finance, RevOps, BI, and other technical teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Establish data-quality checks and exception reporting to identify issues before they affect billing or executive reporting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Maintain an issue log and drive recurring data problems through root-cause analysis and permanent remediation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Consumption Analytics &amp;amp; Reporting&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Create and maintain dashboards showing MSP consumption and business performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Provide reporting at the global, regional, aggregator, partner, tenant, product, and workload levels as appropriate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Track consumption trends, activations, growth, downsell, churn, product mix, and other key MSP performance indicators.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Translate raw consumption data into clear business insights for MSP leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Develop recurring executive reporting that provides a consistent and trusted view of MSP performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Forecasting &amp;amp; Business Intelligence&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Build, maintain, and support MSP forecasting dashboards and underlying data models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Develop consumption-based indicators that improve the accuracy and predictability of ARR forecasts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Track actual consumption and ARR performance against forecast, plan, pacing, and historical trends.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Identify partners, tenants, products, or workloads driving material forecast changes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Provide early-warning indicators for unexpected consumption declines, stalled activations, downsell risk, or unusual growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Support quarter-end forecasting and reconciliation activities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cross-Functional Support&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Act as the primary point of contact for questions regarding MSP consumption data and m3ter reporting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Partner closely with MSP Sales, Finance, RevOps, BI, Engineering, Product, and Deal Desk.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Support investigation of partner billing or consumption questions with clear, data-backed explanations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Translate business requirements from MSP leadership into scalable reporting, metering, and analytics solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Reduce manual reporting and reconciliation through automation wherever practical.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key Deliverables&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success in this role will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Reliable operation and administration of the m3ter platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- High confidence in MSP consumption and billing data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Rapid identification and diagnosis of data discrepancies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- A trusted set of MSP consumption and forecast dashboards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Clear reconciliation between consumption, ARR, forecast, and financial reporting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Automated exception monitoring that identifies issues before they become material.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Reduced manual effort required to produce weekly, monthly, quarterly, and executive MSP reporting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Qualifications&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- 5+ years of experience in data operations, revenue operations, business intelligence, financial operations, SaaS operations, or a related discipline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Strong experience working with consumption-based or usage-based SaaS business models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Experience administering or supporting metering, billing, subscription-management, or revenue platforms; m3ter experience strongly preferred.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Strong SQL and data-analysis skills.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Experience building and maintaining dashboards using modern BI/reporting platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Demonstrated ability to troubleshoot complex data flows across multiple systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Strong understanding of SaaS metrics including ARR, consumption, expansion, contraction, churn, and forecasting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Ability to communicate technical data issues clearly to business and executive stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Strong attention to detail combined with the ability to understand the commercial implications behind the data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Preferred Experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- MSP, MSSP, cloud services, data protection, or cybersecurity experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Usage-based billing or consumption-based pricing experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Experience integrating CRM, billing, telemetry, and financial systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Familiarity with APIs and modern data pipelines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Experience developing automated data-quality and exception-monitoring processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Experience supporting global businesses with multiple currencies, pricing structures, products, and partner models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Within the first 6–12 months, this person should become the single trusted operational owner for MSP metering and consumption intelligence. MSP leadership should be able to answer three questions quickly and confidently:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What are our MSPs consuming?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Is the data correct?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What does it tell us about where the business will land?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role should progressively move Druva&#39;s MSP organization from manual reconciliation and retrospective reporting toward automated monitoring, proactive issue detection, and consumption-driven forecasting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Druva&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Druva is the resilience foundation for the AI enterprise, helping organizations secure and recover from connected risk across data, cyber, identity, and AI. The Resilience Cloud is a fully managed, cloud-native SaaS platform that delivers air-gapped and immutable protection across cloud, SaaS, on-premises, endpoint, and edge environments. Powered by Dru MetaGraph, Druva’s graph-powered intelligence layer, the platform connects critical business context so customers can understand risk, respond faster, recover cleanly, and govern data with greater confidence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Trusted by nearly 7,500 customers, including 75 of the Fortune 500, Druva helps safeguard the critical information and systems businesses depend on in an increasingly connected world.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Visit&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.druva.com/&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;druva.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and follow us on&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/druva/mycompany/&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/druvainc&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/DruvaInc/&quot;&gt;Facebook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;About the Team&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Creative team shapes how a category leader shows up during the most interesting stretch of its story. The problems are real, the audience is smart, the leadership team is invested in creativity, and there&#39;s genuine room to leave a mark on a brand that thousands of enterprises already trust.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Role Purpose &amp;amp; Impact&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Creative Director to own the creative direction and evolution of the Druva brand across everything we make. This is the person who decides how Druva looks, feels, moves, and lands, from the brand system itself to campaigns, video, web, events, product marketing, and the stories our executives tell on the world&#39;s biggest stages.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It&#39;s a rare combination of canvas and craft. You&#39;ll inherit a strong, growing brand in a category that&#39;s being reinvented in real time by AI, and you&#39;ll have the mandate to push it somewhere sharper and braver. You&#39;ll lead our in-house creative team, set the bar for creative excellence, and partner across marketing, product, and leadership to make Druva show up with the clarity and confidence of a company defining what resilience means in the AI era.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re especially excited to meet creative leaders who are AI-forward. These are people who have genuinely rewired how they and their teams work, using AI to compress timelines, expand exploration, and kill the busywork, without ever letting the human craft, taste, and originality slip. We want more ideas and better craft, not faster sameness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role reports to the VP of Corporate Marketing and is based at our Santa Clara headquarters on a hybrid schedule.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the creative direction and evolution of the Druva brand&lt;/strong&gt;, from visual language and motion to tone and expression, ensuring consistency, quality, and ambition across every touchpoint: digital, physical, video, and experiential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead, mentor, and grow the skills of the in-house creative team&lt;/strong&gt;, managing designers, video, and web creative talent while building a culture of craft, collaboration, and creative courage. You&#39;ll develop people, not just approve work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stay hands-on.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll run the studio and get in the file. The best ideas here will often be yours, executed by you, at the level you&#39;re asking of everyone else.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Translate deeply technical concepts into creative that connects&lt;/strong&gt;, turning agentic AI, data security, cyber resilience, and platform architecture into visual storytelling that a CIO, a CISO, and a backup admin all immediately understand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set the AI-forward creative operating model.&lt;/strong&gt; Evaluate, adopt, and responsibly govern AI tools across concepting, production, and iteration; establish clear standards for where AI accelerates the work and where the human hand is non-negotiable; teach the team to use these tools well.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead brand-defining creative moments&lt;/strong&gt;, including product launches, category campaigns, flagship events, and analyst and customer storytelling, from concept through execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Serve as creative partner to our executives&lt;/strong&gt;, shaping keynote visuals, executive storytelling, and thought leadership so our leaders show up with a distinctive, unmistakably Druva point of view.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set the creative direction for druva.com and our digital experience&lt;/strong&gt;, designing web that pops off the page. We want pages people remember: bold, expressive, unmistakably premium, and nothing like the templated enterprise sites we compete against.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own video and motion creative&lt;/strong&gt;, from product explainers and customer stories to brand films and social content, setting the creative vision for animation across channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define the creative vision for Druva&#39;s presence at global events and tradeshows&lt;/strong&gt;, partnering with our events team to deliver immersive, on-brand experiences that people remember after the badge comes off.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner closely with Product Marketing, Corporate Comms, PR, AR, Social, and Demand Gen&lt;/strong&gt;, so the visual and editorial identity move as one system rather than a set of one-offs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Establish and run a clear creative operating model&lt;/strong&gt; covering briefing, intake, review cycles, and quality standards, using Asana to make prioritization, capacity, and status visible to the whole business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage creative resourcing, agency relationships, and production budgets&lt;/strong&gt;, knowing when to build in-house and when to buy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maintain and evolve the Druva brand guidelines and design system&lt;/strong&gt;, keeping them living and usable rather than a PDF nobody opens.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Track and communicate the impact of creative&lt;/strong&gt; on brand awareness, engagement, and campaign performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What Makes You a Great Fit&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;8+ years in brand, creative, or design leadership&lt;/strong&gt;, with proven experience building, leading, and mentoring a multidisciplinary creative team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A portfolio that makes us sit up:&lt;/strong&gt; exceptional creative direction across brand, digital, and video, showing both strategic thinking and execution excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Demonstrated fluency with AI in the creative process:&lt;/strong&gt; a real point of view on which tools earn their place, how to use them responsibly, and how to protect originality and craft while moving significantly faster.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Web design that pops off the page.&lt;/strong&gt; Your portfolio has sites and campaign pages with real visual ambition, the kind that make people stop and look twice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A strong track record translating complex technical concepts into clear, compelling visual storytelling.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deep expertise across brand, campaign, video, and motion creative&lt;/strong&gt;, with the ability to create cohesive experiences across every touchpoint.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exceptional organizational instincts.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ve built creative operating models, intake and review processes, and quality standards that let teams work efficiently at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A sharp editorial eye&lt;/strong&gt; and uncompromising standards for craft, consistency, and creative quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Excellent collaboration and stakeholder management skills&lt;/strong&gt;, with experience influencing across marketing, product, and leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Seniority sufficient to have run a creative studio before, paired with a genuine willingness to stay hands-on&lt;/strong&gt; and execute the work directly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience in fast-paced, high-growth environments&lt;/strong&gt; where the brand is being built and pushed forward, not just maintained.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A real passion for AI and technology&lt;/strong&gt;, and the curiosity to keep learning as the category moves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Ways to Stand Out&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creative leadership experience in AI, SaaS, cloud, cybersecurity, or enterprise infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining or redefining a brand at a high-growth or category-creating company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with executives on keynotes, storytelling, and high-visibility moments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on strength in motion design, experiential, or large-scale event creative&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Web work with a distinct visual signature, ideally including a site redesign or rebrand you led end to end&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with Asana for creative operations, intake, and resourcing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with Figma, Canva and Midjourney&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with technical audiences (IT, security, and infrastructure buyers) and how to create for them without dumbing it down&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience scaling an in-house creative team from lean to full capability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong, well-argued point of view on where brand and AI intersect, and how to use emerging tools responsibly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You’ll Love Working Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Innovation is how we operate, not a side project. You’ll work in a culture that values bold thinking and continuous improvement, where global teams experiment, iterate, and turn new ideas into products customers can rely on.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re looking for high-ownership work, visible impact, and a culture that values innovation, collaboration, accountability, and growth—where you’ll be trusted to lead and empowered to build—you’ll thrive at Druva.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The pay range for this position is expected to be between &lt;strong&gt;$196,000 and $274,667/year;&lt;/strong&gt; however, base pay offered may vary depending on multiple individualized, non-discriminatory factors, including market location, job-related knowledge, skills, and experience. The total compensation package for this position may also include other incentive compensation opportunities in the form of discretionary annual bonus or commissions, and equity. Additionally, full-time employees are eligible to participate in our comprehensive benefits program, including health and wellness benefits, 401(k) retirement plan, life and disability insurance coverages, and other benefits the Company may offer from time to time.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
