&lt;p&gt;Druva is the resilience foundation for the AI enterprise, helping organizations secure and recover from connected risk across data, cyber, identity, and AI. The Resilience Cloud is a fully managed, cloud-native SaaS platform that delivers air-gapped and immutable protection across cloud, SaaS, on-premises, endpoint, and edge environments. Powered by Dru MetaGraph, Druva’s graph-powered intelligence layer, the platform connects critical business context so customers can understand risk, respond faster, recover cleanly, and govern data with greater confidence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Trusted by nearly 7,500 customers, including 75 of the Fortune 500, Druva helps safeguard the critical information and systems businesses depend on in an increasingly connected world.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Visit&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.druva.com/&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;druva.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and follow us on&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/druva/mycompany/&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/druvainc&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/DruvaInc/&quot;&gt;Facebook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be part of a high-impact, fast moving product management team driving our portfolio of data security products serving customer needs around ransomware detection &amp;amp; response, eDiscovery operations, DSPM and agentic AI for data security.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Purpose &amp;amp; Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Director of Product Management to lead execution and team leadership across the data security portfolio of products. This role reports directly to the VP of Product Management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director will act as the operational product leader for the portfolio—owning execution rigor, coaching Product Managers, managing cross-functional alignment, and ensuring that the R&amp;amp;D teams deliver consistent, high-quality outcomes. This is a player–coach role that requires deep engagement with teams, customers, and stakeholders on a daily basis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with customers, analysts and partners to maintain a pulse and point of view on the market&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop vision &amp;amp; product strategy in collaboration with product leaders and executives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build &amp;amp; execute on product roadmap in collaboration with engineering &amp;amp; design teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, mentor and develop a high performing team of product managers /owners&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead regular tracking, analysis of business trends, product engagement metrics and develop insights, actions based on business needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regularly track product engagement metrics, meet with customers and continuously look to optimize for a great product and customer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with pricing team to develop pricing, packaging strategies and track operational metrics for continued evolution of the same&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with GTM teams for product launch, field enablement &amp;amp; other GTM&amp;nbsp; activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regularly engage field field (AEs, SEs, SMEs) teams to support sales opportunities and continuously iterate on supporting GTM machinery to ensure maximum business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes You a Great Fit&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years experience; 8–10 years in product management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing senior PMs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Security domain expertise (EDR/AV, SOC Workflows/Products, GRC workflows/products)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong execution and stakeholder management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical and data-driven&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree required; MBA preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hustler with a keen sense of agency, can-do attitude&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuous learner who has a roll up your sleeves approach to keeping up with the latest in technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like in the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are actively seen as the go-to operational product leader for the data security products by cross functional teams. You are actively driving the R&amp;amp;D roadmap, business impact and are elevating the security PM team in terms of execution rigor, personal skill &amp;amp; career growth. You have a good pulse of the market, customers and can actively see around the corner and drive roadmap, GTM activities accordingly.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You’ll Love Working Here&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Innovation is how we operate, not a side project. You’ll work in a culture that values bold thinking and continuous improvement, where global teams experiment, iterate, and turn new ideas into products customers can rely on.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re looking for high-ownership work, visible impact, and a culture that values innovation, collaboration, accountability, and growth—where you’ll be trusted to lead and empowered to build—you’ll thrive at Druva.&lt;/p&gt;
