&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Druva&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Druva is the resilience foundation for the AI enterprise, helping organizations secure and recover from connected risk across data, cyber, identity, and AI. The Resilience Cloud is a fully managed, cloud-native SaaS platform that delivers air-gapped and immutable protection across cloud, SaaS, on-premises, endpoint, and edge environments. Powered by Dru MetaGraph, Druva’s graph-powered intelligence layer, the platform connects critical business context so customers can understand risk, respond faster, recover cleanly, and govern data with greater confidence.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Trusted by nearly 7,500 customers, including 75 of the Fortune 500, Druva helps safeguard the critical information and systems businesses depend on in an increasingly connected world.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Visit&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.druva.com/&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;druva.com&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and follow us on&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/druva/mycompany/&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://twitter.com/druvainc&quot;&gt;X&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.facebook.com/DruvaInc/&quot;&gt;Facebook&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Office of the CEO sits at the center of Druva&#39;s strategic and operational priorities, partnering closely with the CEO and executive team to drive company-wide initiatives from concept to execution. The team operates as a small, high-trust group that moves fluidly across strategy, operations, and special projects, often stepping in wherever the business needs the most leverage.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Purpose &amp;amp; Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Project Lead, Strategic Planning and Operations, will own a critical portion of the rhythm of the business across three major categories: Business Planning, Strategic Operations, and Strategy. This role operates with significant autonomy, sets the approach for high-stakes cross-functional initiatives, and is trusted to represent the Office of the CEO directly with senior stakeholders. This is a high-impact, high-visibility role reporting into the Office of the CEO, with the latitude to shape how the company plans, decides, and executes at the highest level.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Insights, Decision Support and Analysis:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently drive research and analysis on complex business trends, competitive dynamics, and market conditions to inform CEO- and board-level decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize ambiguous or incomplete data into clear strategic recommendations, proactively identifying risks and opportunities before they&#39;re raised.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a trusted thought partner to senior leaders, shaping strategic narratives rather than simply supporting them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Project Management and Cross-Functional Coordination:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end delivery of the company&#39;s highest-priority, most complex initiatives, often spanning multiple departments, external stakeholders, and ambiguous scope.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set project strategy, timelines, and success metrics with minimal oversight; anticipate roadblocks and course-correct proactively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a primary liaison across departments and with executive stakeholders, resolving cross-functional conflicts and driving alignment at the leadership level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver polished, executive-ready updates directly to the CEO and executive staff, exercising judgment on what to escalate versus own independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Corporate Planning and Alignment: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the design and execution of the corporate operating rhythm (Company All Hands, Quarterly Business Reviews, E-Staff Meetings), including agenda strategy, executive content development, and follow-through on action items.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously improve how the company plans and communicates at the executive level, introducing new frameworks or processes as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes You a Great Fit&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Business Administration, Management, Engineering, or a related field; MBA a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5 years of professional experience, ideally within top-tier consulting, corporate strategy, or a high-growth SaaS environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Established track record of partnering directly with, advising, and influencing senior/executive leadership on high-stakes decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of business operations, strategy development, and SaaS business models, with the judgment to apply that understanding independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to operate with a high degree of autonomy and ambiguity — setting direction, not just executing against it — while maintaining exceptional attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written, verbal, and interpersonal skills; high emotional intelligence and executive presence, with the adaptability to thrive in a fast-paced, high-stakes environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, problem-solving, and decision-making capabilities, including the ability to structure ambiguous problems from scratch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to maintain strict confidentiality and navigate highly sensitive information with integrity and discretion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in Google Workspace, Microsoft Office Suite, and standard modern business tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of AI/LLM-based tools (e.g., Claude, ChatGPT, Gemini, or similar) and how to apply them to accelerate research, synthesis, drafting, and data analysis; comfort evaluating where AI tools can improve the speed and quality of strategic work, and judgment about their limitations in high-stakes or confidential contexts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In the first six months, success will be ramping quickly to understand the Druva business and adding value through strategic analysis and project leadership. Business partners will look to you as a trusted team member. Longer term, success means the corporate operating rhythm runs more effectively because of the frameworks and improvements you&#39;ve introduced, and that you&#39;re recognized as a multiplier for the Office of the CEO&#39;s impact across the company.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
